!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = brain
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Mus musculus
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 10090
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = tissue: brain
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = strain: B6.129S4-Pdgfratm11(EGFP)Sor/J
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = treatment: none
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Tissue frozen with liquid nitrogen was placed between aluminum foil on dry ice and crashed with a hammer. Crushed tissue was placed in Lysis Buffer to extract nuclei and debris was removed using Debris Removal Solution. DAPI was added to the resulting nuclear suspension and DAPI-positive nuclei were sorted and collected using a BD FACS Aria III instrument.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Collected nuclei were washed with PBS containing 1% Bovine Serum Albumin (BSA) and resuspended at the appropriate concentration. Libraries were prepared using the Chromium Next GEM Single Cell 3' Kit v3.1(10x Genomics) according to the manufacturer's protocol.
!Sample_data_processing = Sequencing outputs were demultiplexed using cellranger (6.1.2) mkfastq
!Sample_data_processing = Fastq files were aligned to Mus musculus mm10 reference using cellranger (6.1.2) count
!Sample_data_processing = Assembly: Mouse reference, mm10
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: Processed data files are gzipped cellranger count output directory (filtered_feature_bc_matrix).
